Package: ZICDT
Type: Package
Title: Structure Learning for Directed Trees with Zero-Inflated Compositional Nodes
Version: 0.1.4
Authors@R: person("Shuangjie", "Zhang", email = "sz333024@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Learns directed tree (or forest) structures in which each node is an
    entire zero-inflated composition on the probability simplex. Uses a
    Kullback-Leibler divergence score with a column-stochastic transition-matrix
    mean model, fits edge parameters by an EM algorithm (in C++ via Rcpp),
    searches for the globally optimal spanning arborescence with the
    Chu-Liu/Edmonds algorithm (a virtual root accommodates forests), and selects
    the edge penalty by cross-validation. Implements the method of Zhang et al.
    (directed trees with zero-inflated compositional nodes).
